# The nightly every app here was checked under, and the manifest's `compiler`
# line. Upstream's release notes say "Package and examples built and tested
# with roc nightly-2026-10-23-18478ff". Since 0.9.1 upstream floats the package
# compiler and no longer commits a .roc-version.
#
# 0.10.0 over 0.9.0: no package API changes ("roc bump" reports none for 0.9.1,
# and 0.10.0 says so too). 0.9.1 fixed four parsing bugs and quotes echoed
# argument text in diagnostics. 0.10.0 changes behaviour: everything after a
# subcommand's name is parsed by that subcommand alone, so `work build -q` is
# "The argument \"-q\" was not recognized." when -q is the parent's option.
# The overview and topics/weaver_subcommands.roc say so, and the second was run
# to confirm it. Upstream's own examples moved to basic-cli 0.25.0 and
# `List(OsStr)` at 0.10.0, so the old patch is gone and the plugin pins
# basic-cli 0.25.0 as upstream does. 0.25.0 does not pass the program name in
# `args`. basic-cli 0.26.0 is not used by upstream yet.
compiler nightly-2026-10-23-18478ff

index.json  <- package/, parsed by `roc-syntax-mcp plugin index`. Public and
               private modules; `package [...]` in main.roc is what separates
               them. No source is vendored
examples/   <- examples/, repinned with two edits per file. Upstream pins weaver
               as `../package/main.roc`, a path that resolves only inside a
               checkout, so each header's weaver entry is replaced with the
               0.10.0 tarball above; and each file gains one `##` line above
               its header, because that line is the title
               `list_roc_index(kind: "examples")` prints and upstream's examples
               carry none. Two filenames gain an underscore, because the gate
               reads one flat `<dir>/*.roc`: default-values.roc and
               single-arg.roc. Nothing else differs from upstream.
topics/     <- this package's own, not upstream's: programs written against
               this pin and declared in plugin.json so they answer by name. They
               pin basic-cli 0.25.0, as upstream's examples do.
overview.md <- this package's own. Every API claim on it was compiled, and every
               fenced block appears in verify/overview-snippets.roc.

# Nothing is omitted from the index or examples/. Every upstream example
# flattens and compiles.

# What is not bundled, and why:
#   README.md         its content is in overview.md
#   assets/, scripts/ contributor material, not app-facing
#   .github/          the same

